      "message": "Agreed on `-EBUSY`, and the new comment reads well, thanks. One question on where the check sits: would it be OK to move it below `validate_move_areas()`?\n\nWhen aosp/4312528 added it, both returned `-EINVAL`, so the order didn\u0027t matter. Now a request that `validate_move_areas()` refuses, for example one whose destination isn\u0027t registered with this userfaultfd or whose areas have different protections, gets `-EBUSY` when its slices differ, which tells userspace to copy instead. After `validate_move_areas()`, `-EBUSY` would only reach moves that are otherwise valid.\n\nAs far as I can see, ART ends up in the same place either way: its `EBUSY` fallback, `CopyIoctl()`, gets `ENOENT` for an unregistered range and tolerates it in the same cases as `EINVAL`. So this is only about keeping upstream\u0027s errors for invalid requests.",
